## Why This Is Asked

This scenario tests knowledge of vector DB usage, chunking strategy, latency, and graceful fallback in a realistic but beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-augmented generation
- Document chunking
- Embedding models
- Vector DB indexing and search
- Latency targets and freshness
- Fallback mechanisms

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple chunker
function chunkText(text, maxChars) {
  const chunks = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i += maxChars) {
    chunks.push(text.slice(i, i + maxChars));
  }
  return chunks;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle overlapping chunks to preserve context?
- How would you test latency and accuracy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a candidate’s ability to design end-to-end evaluation for private, privacy-conscious enterprise assistants, focusing on faithfulness, hallucination, and safety under real-world data/versioning constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Grounding to versioned sources and source IDs
- Hallucination detection in live responses
- Privacy safety: PII/secret leakage checks in output and citations
- Performance metrics under load and latency budgets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal evaluation script outline (pseudo)
function evaluate(model, corpus) {
  const prompts = loadPrompts();
  return prompts.map(p => {
    const out = model.respond(p);
    const grounded = ground(out, corpus, p);
    return { prompt: p, output: out, grounded };
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect partial grounding failures (e.g., only some claims anchored)?
- How would you integrate this into a CI/CD pipeline with private data access controls?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of on-device, privacy-preserving ML systems with per-domain adapters that load dynamically while maintaining strict privacy guarantees in a chat application context.

## Key Concepts
- On-device fine-tuning with per-domain adapters
- Dynamic adapter loading from secure knowledge bases
- Adapter injection points (attention vs FFN layers)
- Quantization trade-offs (4-bit vs 8-bit)
- Domain gating and routing strategies
- Memory budgeting for mobile deployment
- Cross-domain evaluation and privacy compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Adapter hub loads domain-specific adapters dynamically
class AdapterHub {
  async loadAdapter(domain) {
    const adapter = await this.secureKB.fetch(domain);
    this.activeAdapters.set(domain, adapter);
  }

  route(query) {
    return this.gatingModel.predict(query);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes production-oriented retrieval design, focusing on multi-tenant privacy, multilingual support, and chunked documents—core competencies for modern media platforms.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation via namespaces
- Hybrid retrieval: lexical BM25 combined with semantic embeddings
- Chunking strategy for long-form transcripts
- Multilingual embeddings with proper normalization
- Vector DB operations, latency targets, observability, and drift handling

## Code Example
